+* Optional `show.numberingDirection: true` offers two equivalent numbering
+  directions of the **same** parent, separately from `chainNavigation`.
+  Current support is 2D-only, with visible interactive naming and a plain,
+  neutral connected acyclic saturated C/H graph without chemical annotations.
+  Both numbered tree signatures must be non-null and equal; uncertain cases
+  keep ordinary numbering and do not expose the control. Signature equality
+  alone is not a general chemical-equivalence test. The live MOL graph must
+  match the numbering graph and have distinct left/right endpoints.
+  The two buttons restore the parent-stem view and reverse copied label order,
+  preserving canonical chain, pool, name and geometry. Explicit component
+  numbering overrides retain priority. Choice is transient across clicks,
+  Update, zoom and resize, resets on step entry/exit or molecule/chain change, and is
+  never exported or stored in quiz progress. Only the opt-in is retained by
+  normalization, Update, duplicate and import/export. Missing/false is off.
+  During presentation Update also preserves this option's authored 2D-only
+  viewer permissions, instead of capturing the underlying free-browse toggles.
